>> title: Beef with Broccoli
>> category: Stir-Fries
>> tags: beef, broccoli, chinese, wok, quick
>> counters: Takeout Counter
>> aka: beef with broccoli, beef and broccoli, broccoli beef, 西蘭花牛肉, xi lan hua niu rou
>> pairs-with: house-brown-sauce, egg-fried-rice
>> servings: 4
>> time: 50 min
>> capacity: 2 — the wok, sear

>> step: velvet, rest 30 min
Toss @flank steak{1%lb}(450 g; sliced 1/4-in thick across the grain) with @egg white{1}, @cornstarch{1%Tbs}, @Shaoxing wine{1%Tbs}, and @baking soda{1/4%tsp}, then ~rest{30%min} in the fridge.

>> step: blanch 1 min, drain dry
Blanch @broccoli{1%lb}(450 g; cut in florets, stems peeled) in boiling salted water for ~boil{1%min}, then drain it and spread it out to dry.

>> step: sear in two batches 3 min, lift out
Sear @&(~2)velveted beef{} in @peanut oil{3%Tbs} in a very hot #wok{}, in two batches so it browns rather than steams, ~sear{3%min} in all, and lift it onto a plate.

>> step: stir-fry the aromatics 1 min
Stir-fry @garlic{3%cloves}(sliced) and @fresh ginger{1%Tbs}(julienned) in the same wok for 20 seconds, then add @&(~2)blanched broccoli{} and ~stirfry{1%min}.

>> step: pour in the sauce, simmer 1 min
Pour @house brown sauce{1%cup}(240 mL) over @&(~1)broccoli{} and ~simmer{1%min} until it clings and turns glossy.

>> step: return the beef, toss
Return @&(~3)seared beef{} to @&(~1)broccoli in sauce{} with whatever juices it gave up, and toss once off the heat.
